/// `v_i` such that
///
/// ```text
/// robust::orient3d(F_i[0], F_i[1], F_i[2], q) > 0
/// ```
///
/// holds **iff** `q` lies on the interior side of face `i` (same side as
/// `v_i`). The query `q` is *inside* the tet iff this holds for all four
/// faces. This is the standard ordering used by visibility-walk point
/// location and by cavity-boundary face identification.
pub(super) const FACE_OUTWARD: [[usize; 3]; 4] = [
    [1, 3, 2], // opposite v0
    [0, 2, 3], // opposite v1
    [0, 3, 1], // opposite v2
    [0, 1, 2], // opposite v3
];

